@startuml database-schema
!theme cerulean
title GupShup Cafe - Database Schema (Entity-Relationship Diagram)

' Hide the circle for relationships
hide circle

' Entity definitions
entity "sessions" as sessions {
  * **id** : TEXT <<PK>>
  --
  * room_id : TEXT
  topic_title : TEXT
  topic_category : TEXT
  participant_count : INTEGER
  started_at : DATETIME
  ended_at : DATETIME
  duration_seconds : INTEGER
  rounds_completed : INTEGER
  created_at : DATETIME
  --
  Stores discussion session metadata
  and analytics information
}

entity "participants" as participants {
  * **id** : TEXT <<PK>>
  --
  * session_id : TEXT <<FK>>
  * user_id : TEXT
  anonymous_name : TEXT
  campus : TEXT
  location : TEXT
  joined_at : DATETIME
  left_at : DATETIME
  speaking_time_seconds : INTEGER
  --
  Tracks individual participants
  within each session
}

entity "topics" as topics {
  * **id** : INTEGER <<PK, AUTO_INCREMENT>>
  --
  * title : TEXT
  description : TEXT
  category : TEXT
  source : TEXT
  used_count : INTEGER
  created_at : DATETIME
  --
  Stores discussion topics and
  tracks their usage statistics
}

' Relationships
sessions ||--o{ participants : "has many"
note on link
  One session can have
  multiple participants
end note

' Additional notes
note right of sessions
  **Session Lifecycle:**
  1. Created when discussion starts
  2. ended_at initially NULL
  3. Updated when discussion ends
  4. duration_seconds calculated
  
  **Key Metrics:**
  - Total duration
  - Number of rounds completed
  - Participant count at end
end note

note right of participants
  **Participant Tracking:**
  - Links users to sessions
  - Stores join/leave times
  - Tracks speaking duration
  - Anonymous for privacy
  
  **User Info:**
  - user_id: unique identifier
  - anonymous_name: display name
  - campus, location: optional
end note

note left of topics
  **Topic Management:**
  - Auto-increment ID
  - Source: 'AI' or 'fallback'
  - used_count incremented each use
  - Categories: Education, Technology,
    Health, Environment, etc.
  
  **Usage Analytics:**
  - Track popular topics
  - Identify trending categories
  - Optimize topic selection
end note

' Index and performance notes
note bottom of sessions
  **Indexes (Recommended):**
  - idx_room_id ON room_id
  - idx_started_at ON started_at
  - idx_ended_at ON ended_at
  
  **Queries:**
  - Recent sessions by started_at DESC
  - Active sessions where ended_at IS NULL
  - Session analytics with participant join
end note

note bottom of participants
  **Indexes (Recommended):**
  - idx_session_id ON session_id
  - idx_user_id ON user_id
  
  **Queries:**
  - Participants per session
  - Unique user count
  - User participation history
end note

note bottom of topics
  **Indexes (Recommended):**
  - idx_category ON category
  - idx_used_count ON used_count
  - idx_source ON source
  
  **Queries:**
  - Most used topics by used_count DESC
  - Topics by category
  - AI vs fallback usage stats
end note

